Caveats:
"1. For CMF 1979-1998, county-level data are not available for individual Alaskan areas before data year 1989. Location code"
"02900 represents all Alaskan areas before 1989. More information: http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#02900."
"2. For CMF 1979-1998, data for the following counties are available beginning in data year data 1994, and thus the 1994"
"population estimates are referenced for cell suppression purposes instead of the 1990 population estimates: Aleutians East"
"Borough (02013), Aleutians West Census Area (02016), Lake and Peninsula Borough (02164), Skagway-Hoonah-Angoon Census Area"
"(02232), Yakutat Borough (02282) Alaska and La Paz (04012), Arizona."
"3. For CMF 1979-1998, data are available for La Paz, Arizona (FIPS code 04012) for 1994-1998. Prior to 1994, death counts and"
"population estimates for La Paz are aggregated with those for Yuma, Arizona (FIPS code 04027). More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#La Paz, Arizona."
"4. For the years 1988 through 1991, if there were three or fewer deaths for a given Georgia county of residence (of deaths"
"occurring in Georgia) with HIV infection (ICD codes *042-*044, 795.8) cited as a cause-of-death (underlying or non-underlying"
"cause), these records were assigned a 'missing' place of residence code, Unknown County (code 13999). These deaths do not appear"
"in county death rates, but these deaths are included in the state and national death rates. More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Unknown, Georgia."
"5. Data for Kalawao, Hawaii (FIPS code 15005) are available beginning in 1989. More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#15005."
"6. For the 1979-1998 CMF, death counts and population for Cibola county, New Mexico (FIPS code 35006) are available beginning"
"with data year 1989. For data years 1979-1988, deaths and population counts for Cibola county are aggregated with Valencia"
"county, New Mexico (FIPS code 35061). More information: http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Cibola, New Mexico."
"7. Deaths and population estimates are reported separately for Baltimore City (FIPS code 24510) and county (FIPS code 24005)."
"8. Deaths and population estimates are shown separately from the adjacent counties for Carson City, Nevada (FIPS code 32510)."
"9. Deaths for the city of Columbus, GA (previous FIPS code 13510) have been aggregated with Muscogee county, GA (FIPS code"
"13215)."
"10. Deaths and population estimates are reported separately for St. Louis City (FIPS code 29510) and county (FIPS code 29189)."
"11. Death rates are flagged as Unreliable when the rate is calculated with a numerator of 20 or less. More information:"
"http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Unreliable."
"12. The population figures used in the calculation of death rates for the age group 'under 1 year' are the live births for the"
"given time period. More information: http://wonder.cdc.gov/wonder/help/cmf.html#Age Group."
"13. Population figures in this table for 1979 and 1981-89 are intercensal estimates of the July 1 resident population of the"
"United States. Note that the state and county population estimates for these years are not consistent with national estimates."
"The population figures in this table for 1980 and 1990 are modified age-race-sex (MARS) April 1 census counts. The population"
"figures for 1991-98 are bridged-race intercensal estimates of the July 1 resident population."